        "content": "<p>avanhatt opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14789\">PR #14789</a> from <code>avanhatt:veri-simd-canary</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Add support in the ISLE verifier for SIMD types with explicit lane counts. This allows us to catch ISLE rules that should exclude vector types but do not (e.g., #14566, #14631, #14701). </p>\n<p>Introduce <code>lanemap</code> and similar forms into the ISLE spec lang, update CLIF terms to use these to indicate when specs apply per lane (e.g., <code>iadd</code> does not carry between lanes), add support for vector types into inference and the verifier. Add new veri filetests.</p>\n<p>Note the <code>Type</code> model change alters most SMT queries, so this will be slow on the CI cache. </p>\n</blockquote>",
